# AWE Phase Machine

## The 8 phases

| # | Phase | What happens | Human gate? |
|---|-------|--------------|-------------|
| 1 | `intake` | Ticket pulled (or pasted), sanitized into a structured spec, open questions collected in `plans/<ticket>/open-questions.md`. | Answers questions asynchronously by editing `open-questions.md`. |
| 2 | `architect` | Architect: optional `docs/awe/` briefing (skip missing) then root-grain graph → high-level `architecture.md` with a mandatory **Decision surface** (product-level decisions — input constraints, placement/business logic, ownership, edge cases, scope — decided-with-rationale or asked as options with trade-offs), gherkin E2E, `<role>.spec.md` (`backend` / `frontend` / `fullstack`, no file lists). May update `docs/awe/` if this ticket taught a lasting domain fact; skip if not. | Reads the spec; answers architect questions if any. |
| 3 | `approve` | `/awe-approve` validates any architect questions, then flips **specs** to `approved` after an explicit human **yes**. | **HARD GATE.** Nothing codes without this. |
| 4 | `code` | Per role (`backend` / `frontend` / `fullstack`): branch `awe/<ticket>-<role>` (worktree **only** if another plan is already implementing), coder writes `implementation.plan.md` + `implementation-questions.md`, **stops if questions are open or `dependsOn` is unmet**, then TDD — **including the Playwright e2e specs** under `plans/<ticket>/e2e/` (gherkin → spec 1:1, written to the recording quality bar in `smoke-e2e.md`). Source writes are hook-blocked until questions are checked and dependencies are `done`. | Answers implementation questions. |
| 5 | `review` | Scanners run; `awe-reviewer` reviews the diff (optional `awe-security-reviewer` when `securityReview: true`); findings in `reviews/round-<N>.md`. Coder records `round-<N>-response.md` (fixed / rebutted / deferred). `needs-fix` → respawn coder; `verified` → next phase. | Intervenes on any finding. |
| 6 | `smoke` | `awe-smoke-tester` **runs the coder's Playwright specs** (architect Gherkin/AC, 1:1) on **localhost** — it never writes test code; missing, stale, or under-demonstrating specs bounce to the coder. Browser video for UI must **visibly show the full journey and the outcome** (scroll + dwell per `smoke-e2e.md`); API trace for backend; **HTML report** is the combined viewer. `needs-fix` respawns the coder (`smokeIteration`, same budget as review). On green: report + `run-smoke.sh` + numbered human steps in `smoke.md` and the smoke-folder README. | **HARD GATE.** Human watches the HTML report (optional hand-run), then `signed: true` + initials + date. |
| 7 | `ship` | `/awe-ship` pre-flight (signoff + fresh evidence + clean scanners), commit, push `awe/<ticket>-*` branch, open PR via MCP or printed commands. Then a knowledge pass (`docs/awe/**` + `manage_adr`) if a lasting decision was made. | Merges the PR. |
| 8 | post-merge E2E | Combined end-to-end run on the base branch. Regressions re-enter via `/awe-regression` as `plans/<ticket>-R<N>/`. | Confirms production behavior. |

Phases are **per ticket**. Another ticket in `approve` does not freeze source writes for a ticket that is already in `code`.

## Allowed actions per phase (hard-enforced by hooks, per ticket)

| Phase | Write code | Write `plans/<ticket>/` | `git push` | Spawn dev subagent | Spawn reviewer |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| intake / architect / approve | ❌ hook denies | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |
| code | ✅ (role scope) | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ (approved plan only) | ✅ |
| review | ✅ (fixes) | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ (fix rounds) | ✅ |
| smoke | ❌ (plans + `.cursor/state` only) | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ (bounce to `code` first) | ❌ |
| ship | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ (gated: signoff + evidence + branch) | ❌ | ❌ |

## State file — `.cursor/state/awe-state.json`

Only `/awe-*` skills (including `/awe-run`) write this file. Multiple tickets may be in-flight. Top-level `ticket`/`phase`/`roles` are the **session focus**; `tickets` is the source of truth. Legacy files with only the top-level fields still work (hooks synthesize a one-entry map).

```json
{
  "active": true,
  "ticket": "PROJ-123",
  "phase": "intake|architect|approve|code|review|smoke|ship|done",
  "roles": {
    "backend":  { "planStatus": "draft|questions-open|approved", "iteration": 0, "verified": false },
    "frontend": { "planStatus": "draft|questions-open|approved", "iteration": 0, "verified": false },
    "fullstack": { "planStatus": "draft|questions-open|approved", "iteration": 0, "verified": false }
  },
  "dependsOn": [],
  "tickets": {
    "PROJ-123": {
      "phase": "code",
      "roles": { "backend": { "planStatus": "approved", "iteration": 0, "verified": false } },
      "dependsOn": [],
      "smokeIteration": 0
    },
    "PROJ-124": {
      "phase": "architect",
      "roles": { "frontend": { "planStatus": "draft", "iteration": 0, "verified": false } },
      "dependsOn": ["PROJ-123"]
    }
  },
  "updatedAt": "<ISO-8601>"
}
```

- `active: false` (or a missing file) means **AWE does not interfere at all** — every hook exits immediately. Shipping one ticket sets `active: false` only when no other ticket is still in-flight.
- `dependsOn` lists other plan ids. Intake is never blocked. **Application source** is denied until every listed ticket is `phase: done` (or has left state).
- `iteration` counts completed **review** rounds for that role on that ticket.
- `smokeIteration` (ticket-level, default 0) counts Playwright SMOKE ↔ coder rounds. Same budget as `reviewIterations`, independent of review. Legacy `verifyIteration` is still read.
- `verified` on a role flips true only on a reviewer's `verified` verdict. Human SMOKE signoff is `awe-signoff.json`.

## Evidence contract — `.cursor/state/awe-evidence.json`

Written by the coding agent after running the discovered or configured test command (`commands.test` from `.cursor/state/awe-discovered.json` or optional `awe.config.json`), and refreshed after every fix round:

```json
{ "testsPassed": true, "command": "npm test", "at": "<ISO-8601>" }
```

The `stop` hook demands evidence younger than **2 hours** before it lets a code/review session end (unit/test command) and before it lets a smoke session end (Playwright: `awe-smoke-evidence.json`). Stale or missing evidence forces the agent to re-run instead of claiming done.

This evidence is the machine-checkable slice of the standing **Definition of Done** — see `.cursor/skills/references/definition-of-done.md`. The DoD is the full bar (correctness, quality, integration, docs, ship-readiness); `awe-evidence.json` proves the CODE Correctness slice. SMOKE adds `awe-smoke-evidence.json` (Playwright Gherkin on localhost, HTML report + video/trace). AWE never treats "tests pass" alone as done.

## SMOKE evidence — `.cursor/state/awe-smoke-evidence.json`

Written by the smoke tester after a green Playwright run. `command` must be portable (no sandbox browser paths). `htmlReport` is the combined viewer:

```json
{
  "playwrightPassed": true,
  "command": "npx playwright test -c plans/PROJ-123/e2e",
  "htmlReport": ".cursor/state/smoke/PROJ-123-html-report",
  "video": ".cursor/state/smoke/PROJ-123/…webm",
  "trace": ".cursor/state/smoke/PROJ-123/…zip",
  "at": "<ISO-8601>"
}
```

## Human signoff — `.cursor/state/awe-signoff.json`

Written by the human (or by the `/awe-smoke` skill confirming the human's edit to `smoke.md`):

```json
{ "verified": true, "initials": "MA", "at": "<ISO-8601>" }
```

`git push` in the ship phase is blocked until this exists with `verified: true`.

## Iteration budget semantics

`reviewIterations` (default 3) is a **hard budget per ticket per loop**, not a suggestion. Review uses `roles.<role>.iteration`. SMOKE uses ticket `smokeIteration` (Playwright needs-fix → coder). While the matching counter is below the budget, `needs-fix` respawns the coder with findings in `handoff.md`. When the budget is reached without a pass, the pipeline writes `plans/<ticket>/ESCALATION.md` and stops for a human. The budget exists so a stuck loop bothers a human instead of burning tokens.

## Orchestration

Default is **auto**: `/awe-run` (or a natural-language task that invokes it) chains intake → architect → code → review. APPROVE and SMOKE remain human stops. Individual `/awe-*` skills still work. `awe.config.json` is optional.
